**A is <3-chlorobutan-2-one>, $\mathrm{CH_3C(=O)CH(Cl)CH_3}$.** Counting <chlorine> as one <hydrogen> in the index of <index of hydrogen deficiency> gives $(2\times4+2-7-1)/2=1$. A single <carbonyl> accounts for that unsaturation; the resonance at $203.2$ ppm identifies a <ketone>, while the $59.0$ ppm methine bears <chlorine>.

The <carbon-13 NMR> assignments are $\delta_C=203.2$ for $\mathrm{C=O}$, $25.7$ for $\mathrm{CH_3CO}$, $59.0$ for $\mathrm{CHCl}$ and $20.1$ ppm for $\mathrm{CH(Cl)CH_3}$. The four distinct <carbon> environments agree with the unsymmetrical structure. The small signal near 77 ppm belongs to the usual deuterated chloroform <solvent>, rather than to a fifth <carbon> of A.

= ii
{parent=a}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=ii}

The strong $1724\,\mathrm{cm^{-1}}$ absorption is the <carbonyl stretching vibration> of a saturated <ketone>. Its exact <wavenumber> depends on substitution and measurement conditions; the important discrimination is that it is far below the high-frequency <acyl chloride> band in B and is accompanied by a <carbonyl> <carbon-13 NMR> resonance near 200 ppm.

= iii
{parent=a}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=iii}

Write the proton-labelled structure as $\mathrm{CH_3^{a}C(=O)CH^{b}(Cl)CH_3^{c}}$. The assignments are
$$
\begin{array}{c|c|c|c}
\text{site}&\delta_H/\mathrm{ppm}&\text{integral}&\text{multiplicity}\\\hline
a&2.334&3&\text{singlet}\\
b&4.3365&1&\text{quartet}\\
c&1.6065&3&\text{doublet}
\end{array}
$$
The <NMR quartet> is centred at $(4.371+4.302)/2=4.3365$ ppm; each adjacent line differs by $0.023$ ppm. The <NMR doublet> has the same spacing, $1.618-1.595=0.023$ ppm. At 300 MHz,
$$
\boxed{{}^3J_{bc}=300(0.023)=6.9\,\mathrm{Hz}.}
$$
Three equivalent methyl <protons> split $b$ into a $1:3:3:1$ <NMR quartet>; the single methine <proton> splits $c$ into a $1:1$ <NMR doublet>. No resolved <long-range scalar coupling> splits the acetyl methyl, giving its <NMR singlet>. The integrals total seven <protons>.

\Image[paper-1-chloroketone-assignment.png]
{title=Independent original carbon and proton assignments for A, with the measured methine–methyl coupling}

